# .csv to store UE's information in HSS
# Kept in the following format: "Name,Auth,IMSI,Key,OP_Type,OP/OPc,AMF,SQN,QCI,IP_alloc"
#
# Name:     Human readable name to help distinguish UE's. Ignored by the HSS. Must be unique.
# Auth:     Authentication algorithm used by the UE. Valid algorithms are XOR
#           (xor) and MILENAGE (mil)
# IMSI:     UE's IMSI value
# Key:      UE's key (Ki), where other keys are derived from. Stored in hexadecimal.
#           MUST match the key programmed inside the SIM card.
# OP_Type:  Operator's code type, either OP or OPc
# OP/OPc:   Operator Code/Cyphered Operator Code, stored in hexadecimal.
#           MUST match the card.
# AMF:      Authentication management field, stored in hexadecimal
# SQN:      UE's Sequence number for freshness of the authentication.
#           If attach starts failing after many connects, bump it and restart.
# QCI:      QoS Class Identifier for the UE's default bearer.
# IP_alloc: IP allocation stratagy for the SPGW.
#           With 'dynamic' the SPGW will automatically allocate IPs
#           With a valid IPv4 (e.g. '172.16.0.2') the UE will have a statically assigned IP.
#
# Note: Lines starting by '#' are ignored and will be overwritten
# Note: keep one empty line at end of file, srsRAN HSS requires it.
#
# ---- example card (IMSI 001010123456789 => MCC 001, MNC 01) ----
# Replace Key/OPc with the values programmed in YOUR card, or add rows
# via /writesim (auto-appends) or /userupload. /start with mcc=001 mnc=01.
ue0,mil,001010123456789,00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff,opc,63bfa50ee6523365ff14c1f45f88737d,8001,000000001234,7,dynamic
# ---- spare slot example (comment out / delete if unused) ----
# ue1,mil,001010123456790,00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff,opc,63bfa50ee6523365ff14c1f45f88737d,8001,000000001235,7,dynamic

